From d2a087b85d5e0a26e56d9291f47dc1465024eebc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:05:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] fix(audio): count an XMA frame whose header straddles
 the packet end

GetPacketInfo walks the frames that begin in a packet. When fewer than
15 bits are left, the next frame's header continues in the following
packet and the walk stopped without counting that frame. The caller then
took the frame before it for the packet's last one, and when the read
offset sat on the straddling frame it saw frame 0 with size 0 of a packet
whose frame count did not include it, so it skipped the frame instead of
assembling its header from both packets. The XMA2 header count covers
part of this, but not packets whose header count matches the frames
found before the straddling one, and not XMA1 packets, which carry no
count.

Port Xenia Canary's handling (src/xenia/apu/xma_context_new.cc,
XmaContextNew::GetPacketInfo, at 451f915): when bits remain, count the
frame and, if the read offset is on it, report it as the current frame
with size 0. Decode already reads a size-0 frame's header from the two
packets combined.

Project Gotham Racing 4's menu music streams contain such frames; the
MTR-PGR4 port carries the same change as its menu split-frame fix.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/audio/xma_context.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/xma_context.cpp b/src/audio/xma_context.cpp
index 11b83be..fa80672 100644
--- a/src/audio/xma_context.cpp
+++ b/src/audio/xma_context.cpp
@@ -359,6 +359,17 @@ kPacketInfo XmaContext::GetPacketInfo(uint8_t* packet, uint32_t frame_offset) {
 
   while (true) {
     if (stream.BitsRemaining() < kBitsPerFrameHeader) {
+      // This frame's 15-bit header runs into the next packet, so its size
+      // isn't readable yet. Count it anyway, or the caller takes the previous
+      // frame for the packet's last and skips straight past this one. Size 0
+      // sends it to the split-header path.
+      if (stream.BitsRemaining() > 0) {
+        if (stream.offset_bits() == frame_offset) {
+          packet_info.current_frame_ = packet_info.frame_count_;
+          packet_info.current_frame_size_ = 0;
+        }
+        packet_info.frame_count_++;
+      }
       break;
     }
 
